{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1775990120,"nonce":"Pfrd3zhu1Olq85vNQGOrHF+oO0s=","title":"Redact secrets from exception logs in notifiers","message":"## Problem\n\nTelegram bot token and webhook URLs are logged in plaintext when HTTP requests fail:\n\n```\n2026-03-12 02:33:29,033 [adapters.notifiers.telegram] WARNING: Telegram: HTTPSConnectionPool(host='api.telegram.org', port=443): Max retries exceeded with url: /bot8367824483:AAEnnIQeRDv-F6V9NxUYAwzvdxsqXc4Ef5E/getUpdates?...\n```\n\n`requests.RequestException` includes the full URL in its message. When logged directly, secrets are exposed.\n\n## Files\n\n- `adapters/notifiers/telegram.py` lines 54, 79, 105\n- `adapters/notifiers/webhook.py` line 31\n\n## Tests\n\n- `tests/test_telegram_notifier.py::test_exception_log_redacts_token`\n  Assert: when notify() fails, logged message contains `/bot\u003cREDACTED\u003e/` not the actual token\n- `tests/test_webhook_notifier.py::test_exception_log_redacts_url`\n  Assert: when notify() fails, logged message contains `?\u003cPARAMS\u003e` not actual query string\n\n## Implementation\n\n1. Add `_redact_url()` helper to `adapters/notifiers/_utils.py`:\n   ```python\n   import re\n   \n   def redact_url(e: Exception) -\u003e str:\n       \"\"\"Redact URLs from exception messages.\"\"\"\n       msg = str(e)\n       msg = re.sub(r'/bot[^/]+/', '/bot\u003cREDACTED\u003e/', msg)  # Telegram tokens\n       msg = re.sub(r'\\?[^\\s)]+', '?\u003cPARAMS\u003e', msg)  # Query strings\n       return msg\n   ```\n\n2. Update logging in telegram.py and webhook.py to use `redact_url(e)` instead of `e`\n\n## Patterns to follow\n\nSee `adapters/notifiers/_utils.py` for existing shared utilities.\n\n## REQ\n\nREQ-019 (observability — logs should not leak secrets)","files":null}]}